# Proposed guideline changes — `docs/testing.md`

**Goal:** make `docs/testing.md` the real source-of-truth backing the Vanta test "Production data not used for dev or test" (ISO 27001 A.8.31 / A.8.33), so renewal evidence is a true engineering doc, not a self-authored memo.

**Repo:** `normainofficial/normain` · file `docs/testing.md`

## Change 1 — add a "Test Data Management" section

Append this new top-level section (after "Writing Tests"):

```markdown
## Test Data Management

Development and test environments never use production data. All non-production data is
synthetic.

- **Local development** runs against local Docker Postgres/Redis (see the Development Guide).
  The database is populated by the seed script
  (`src/apps/server/tenant-api/src/database/seed.ts`), which uses the open-source
  `drizzle-seed` library to generate deterministic, fictional records (e.g. a single
  "Dev Tenant"). No production data is ever exported or imported.
- **Automated tests** build their own in-test fixtures. AI evaluation tests use checked-in
  synthetic fixtures (`src/apps/server/worker/src/extractInsightWorker/exhaustiveEvalFixtures`).
  No production data is referenced.
- **Environment separation** — `development` and `production` are provisioned as separate
  Terraform stacks (`terraform/environments/app-development` vs `app-production`) with
  separate resource groups, storage accounts, databases, and database-access groups
  (`sg_normain_dev_db_accessor` vs `sg_normain_prod_db_accessor`). No database server is
  shared between environments, so production data cannot flow into dev/test.
```

## What this deliberately does NOT say
- **No "proprietary seeding solution."** That claim (in the old `QAAndTesting.jpg` memo) is
  not true — seeding is the open-source `drizzle-seed` library. Removed.
- **No E2E test layer.** `testing.md` already correctly states E2E/Playwright does not exist.
  The old memo's E2E claim is dropped by using this doc as evidence instead.

